{"title":"2017 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A snowman is built by stacking three spheres with their centres aligned vertically. The spheres have radii of 10 cm, 20 cm and 30 cm.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>How tall is the snowman?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/c/c5cd64484a16e04c49ac26e4fcc3927c3704b779.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 90 \\text{ cm} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 100 \\text{ cm} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 110 \\text{ cm} \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 120 \\text { cm} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 130 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"603\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the radii are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/8/1c82d27f870d92847be4cd156984a330795f1716.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/7/047576451357c4cec7019ecb44495dc7fc75eb46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/5/665d4ca6471d70415a61cbec47f7886c3abaa582.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />, the diameters are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/9/da9f4b766559527b6ba4f859ced06c1a971371ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\text{ cm} \\times 2 = 20 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"147\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50f82e7005d32bcf5b2e8122d9c82e9fb799d2e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 \\text { cm} \\times 2 = 40 \\text { cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"147\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/9/fe9447d4098e46cf3b774c56526c53195373aa1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30 \\text { cm} \\times 2 = 60 \\text { cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"147\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the snowman must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/7/5b7e1e7b562898bcc991660fdcdeaa472f759a92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 \\text { cm} + 40 \\text{ cm} + 60 \\text{ cm} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 120 \\text { cm}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"306\" height=\"30\" /> tall.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2017 CEMC Cayley\">2017 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC Cayley Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp